1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,128
<i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪</i>

2
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:06,673
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,844
<i>- ♪ Fix it ♪</i>
<i>- ♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪</i>

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,762
<i>♪ Holding the scissors ♪</i>

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
<i>♪ One cut, and it's over ♪</i>

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,351
Come here, give me a kiss.

7
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:20,311
Hey! Stop that!

8
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,189
So, I'm semi-rejected by you now, huh?

9
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,983
[Chiquita] <i>What's your group's name?</i>

10
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:25,984
Oh, we are the…

11
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:30,155
[all] Karayom Kweens!

12
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,072
And your name is?

13
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,532
Chiquita?!

14
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,534
You stole my boyfriend.

15
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:35,952
I'm prettier than you!

16
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,203
[jeering]

17
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:39,622
No matter what, we need to beat them.

18
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:40,832
[Velma] <i>I got you.</i>

19
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,250
What do you need?

20
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,335
There are missing children,

21
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:47,088
and we suspect
they were taken to Velora Bay.

22
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:50,008
[Emerson] <i>We need to win</i>
<i>this contest to get there.</i>

23
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,718
I don't believe you.

24
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:54,012
No. What I'm saying is true.

25
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,388
[Chiquita] <i>Step aside.</i>

26
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:58,266
- [audience cheering]
- [Trinity] <i>This is the fiercest,</i>

27
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:01,019
<i>and the most fabulous</i>

28
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:03,605
drag showdown of the year,

29
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,565
the Reyna Royale Rumble!

30
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:07,358
[audience cheering]

31
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,569
[Tiny] The Glitter Bombz!

32
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:10,612
[thuds]

33
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:13,114
[audience cheering]

34
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:16,242
PREVIOUSLY

35
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:20,163
- [thudding]
- [audience whooping]

36
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,247
Come on!

37
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,249
Let's welcome to the stage…

38
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,670
The Karayom Kweens!

39
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:30,381
[audience cheering]

40
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,884
[music continues]

41
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,272
Looks like we'll have a tough time.

42
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:49,943
[in English] This is the moment
we've all been waiting for.

43
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:54,489
With a jaw-breaking score of 92.7…

44
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:56,825
Oh, my god! I'm so nervous!

45
00:01:56,908 --> 00:02:00,120
- [audience cheering]
- [Trinity laughing]

46
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,039
[Atoy] <i>Give this to us, Lord.</i>

47
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,208
<i>I just want my children back.</i>

48
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:08,253
<i>I just want a chance</i>
<i>to rebuild our family.</i>

49
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:09,170
[music fades]

50
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:11,506
It's none other than…

51
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,508
[Velma] Karayom Kweens!

52
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:15,218
[rousing music playing]

53
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:20,014
And still the reigning queens
of Royale Rumble!

54
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,225
The Glitter Bombz!

55
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:23,351
Come on!

56
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:24,727
[exclaiming]

57
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:27,856
[Trinity] Congratulations,
The Glitter Bombz!

58
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,858
Wow! Still the champion!

59
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,317
[Trinity chuckles]

60
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:34,612
Congratulations, The Glitter Bombz!

61
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,865
[audience applauding]

62
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:40,076
[theme music playing]

63
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,995
[motorcycle revving]

64
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:42,954
[sewing machine whirring]

65
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:44,873
[scratches]

66
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:45,915
[snipping]

67
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:49,794
[sewing machine clacking]

68
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,963
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

69
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:53,756
[thumps & gunshots]

70
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,466
- [music intensifies]
- [clicking]

71
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,552
[snipping]

72
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:59,721
[music swells]

73
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,435
[music fades]

74
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:06,978
[muffled chatter in the distance]

75
00:03:07,061 --> 00:03:10,565
[in English] And I beg to disagree!

76
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:16,112
They can't win,
because someone lost their life earlier…

77
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:18,239
- Right!
- …in their performance!

78
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:20,491
[jeering]

79
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,035
My goodness!

80
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:23,995
What now, Velma?

81
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:25,496
Shut up! Rawr!

82
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:29,500
It's in the rules of this competition

83
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:36,382
that no animals should be harmed!

84
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:38,760
Eh, what's this?

85
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:40,678
[audience] Ohh!

86
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:42,138
[audience] Whoa!

87
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,015
Look, everyone!

88
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:47,018
[awing & gasping]

89
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,979
I saw under the table earlier

90
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:55,735
the pitiful and lifeless dove
used in your performance.

91
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:59,030
- [music swells]
- [awing & gasping]

92
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:00,698
[music continues]

93
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:02,825
It's dead!

94
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,828
[jeering]

95
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:08,748
This is animal cruelty!

96
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:11,542
And they should be disqualified!

97
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:12,585
Right!?

98
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,962
- [jeering]
- [music swells]

99
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:15,338
That's right!

100
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:17,632
What's the use of having talent
if it won't wake up ever again?!

101
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,094
[squeals]

102
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:23,137
Shut up!

103
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,932
You jealous frogs!

104
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:31,145
You're just envious because we won!

105
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:33,314
- [audience] Ohh!
- You shut up, huh!

106
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:36,359
Because rules are not meant to be broken!

107
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:38,319
Hey! I'll break your ugly face!

108
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:40,154
[jeering]

109
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:42,573
[sneaky music playing]

110
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,492
Try it, girl!

111
00:04:44,575 --> 00:04:46,494
Uh-huh! Hmm.

112
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:48,454
That's probably why
you're three-time champions,

113
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,707
because you're cheaters!

114
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,584
- [Nestor] Right! Cheaters!
- [Emerson] You're cheaters!

115
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,336
[Trinity] Okay! Wait, wait, wait!

116
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,213
Listen, listen!

117
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,674
Okay, okay.

118
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:01,301
We have a decision.

119
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:04,554
Because the rules were violated…

120
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:09,976
we declare that
Karayom Kweens is the winner!

121
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:14,689
- [audience cheering]
- [sneaky music playing]

122
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:20,403
Congratulations, Karayom Kweens!

123
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:23,156
- [audience cheering]
- [music continues]

124
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,825
Rules are rules! Okay?

125
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:27,410
So, no fighting.

126
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:28,953
Because at the end of the day,

127
00:05:29,037 --> 00:05:31,706
you're all beautiful, you're all talented!

128
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:33,791
- [Emerson] Yes!
- They're all amazing!

129
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,126
Don't you think?

130
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:36,169
[audience] Yes!

131
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:40,423
Right? So once again, give it up for…

132
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:42,550
The Karayom Kweens!

133
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:46,345
- [audience cheering]
- [sneaky music playing]

134
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:51,893
Thank you.
Because of this, I can save my kids.

135
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,936
- [audience cheering]
- Let's stand by this, okay?

136
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,897
- Of course, of course.
- Okay.

137
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,523
- [Nestor] Game.
- [Emerson] Let's go.

138
00:05:57,607 --> 00:06:01,319
[all] Karayom Kweens!

139
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:04,822
- [audience cheering]
- [music continues]

140
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,949
Can you believe it, we actually won!

141
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:09,410
Oh, you know,
I still can't believe we're the winners.

142
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:12,121
Yes. And thank goodness,
the Lord heard our prayer earlier.

143
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,748
- [Gavin] Right.
- Yes.

144
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,416
We're amazing,
we're amazing, we're amazing.

145
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,252
- [Paldo] I still can't believe it.
- Congratulations!

146
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:20,046
[Emerson] My prayer earlier was heard.

147
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:21,547
- [audience cheering]
- [Trinity] There!

148
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,383
Thank you! Thank you!

149
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:26,803
[audience cheering]

150
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:30,723
Once again, our new champion!

151
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:34,185
The Karayom Kweens take the stage!

152
00:06:34,268 --> 00:06:36,145
[audience cheering]

153
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:39,107
[audience] Karayom Kweens! Karayom Kweens!

154
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,193
[exclaiming & laughing]

155
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:44,695
[music continues]

156
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:47,406
Oh! Brother Kurt, hold this!

157
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:49,325
[phone ringing]

158
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:53,663
- [all] Karayom Kweens!
- Hello?

159
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:56,374
- Hello-- Audrey?
- [all] Karayom Kweens!

160
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:58,668
- Huh?!
- [Emerson] Take our picture!

161
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:01,504
Take our picture!
You, you, you, take our picture here.

162
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:03,005
- Take our picture.
- [action music playing]

163
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:04,674
That's it, that's it,
that's it, take our picture.

164
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:05,925
That's it, that's it.

165
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:06,843
[lively chatter & cheering]

166
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,053
- [phone rings]
- [grunts]

167
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,098
[in English] Hello, Mr. Red Regalia!

168
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:16,102
Yes. Mr. Kalaf is sick today,
so he's resting.

169
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:18,354
Yes.

170
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:21,899
But he's expecting you to wire transfer
his payment tonight.

171
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,192
No delays allowed.

172
00:07:23,901 --> 00:07:24,902
Okay. Will do that.

173
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,823
Mr. Kalaf
will expect your delivery on his birthday.

174
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:33,202
Okay? So, your goods
are in one of the villas, right?

175
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:36,998
You will see Mr. Kalaf at Velora Bay.

176
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:40,001
Bring your wife, Sir Red.

177
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,294
She will enjoy it there.

178
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,463
Okay. Give my regards to Boss K, okay?

179
00:07:43,546 --> 00:07:47,842
I will. So, if there are
any requests, just call me.

180
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:49,177
Thank you.

181
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:51,137
Wait. I'm going to send you
a picture. Okay?

182
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,973
[suspicious music playing]

183
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:58,394
[Red on the phone] <i>Watch him.</i>

184
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,521
He might try to infiltrate Velora Bay.

185
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:02,231
That's a problem.

186
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,566
[Trinity on the phone] <i>I don't know him.</i>

187
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:06,527
But I'll forward this
to the head of security.

188
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,571
Don't worry, sir.

189
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:12,450
No undesirables have
entered Boss K's island.

190
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:15,578
If he shows up,
he will be killed on the spot,

191
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:20,291
and his body fed
to Boss K's crocodile pets.

192
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,127
- Thank you.
<i>- All right, Mr. Regalia.</i>

193
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,963
[music swells]

194
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:28,049
Oh, well! Not that I'm bragging, okay?

195
00:08:28,132 --> 00:08:31,802
But if not for me,
we wouldn't be able to beat Glitter Bombz!

196
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,555
- [woman] Oh! Right!
- Thanks, Ma! Thanks!

197
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,806
- [lively chatter]
- [Velma] You're welcome!

198
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,850
And because of that, I'm buying drinks!

199
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:39,560
- Whoa!
- [lively chatter]

200
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:40,853
Pineapple!

201
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,230
- [exclaims]
- Yes!

202
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:45,107
- [woman] That's right! That's right!
- I thought… you're alcohol-free now.

203
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:46,108
[Nestor] No!

204
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,152
- Just kidding, just kidding.
- Oh, that's enough!

205
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:49,987
Better for us to chat in Tabang Lupa.

206
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,572
- Okay!
- Okay, oh.

207
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:52,740
Wait.

208
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:54,742
Where are Brother Atoy and Papa Uno?

209
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,662
[sneaky music playing]

210
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:58,704
[Nestor] Where are they?

211
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:00,831
Two access points.

212
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,126
Via helicopter, via boat.

213
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:07,922
But because of that radar tower,

214
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:11,384
we can't enter without being detected.

215
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:15,304
That means we can't deploy
first strikers here,

216
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:19,517
because even a pump boat will be spotted.

217
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:26,315
The only way is to disable their radar
and communication systems.

218
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:29,485
Sir…

219
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:31,988
I can infiltrate that.

220
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:39,537
I just need step-by-step instructions
to hack their computers.

221
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:42,957
That will be the easy part of the job,

222
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,419
because our IT team already
prepared for it.

223
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:49,088
All you have to do…

224
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:52,675
is plug this into their computer.

225
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:55,177
[music continues]

226
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:59,056
Once you do that,

227
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:02,351
our IT team can access their system.

228
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:06,272
Nice. Plug and play.

229
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:08,232
[Mercado] Now…

230
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:14,739
my biggest concern is that
the people with you are not trained.

231
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:16,032
[action music playing]

232
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:18,492
This is very risky.

233
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:20,870
They must follow protocol,

234
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:22,663
even if they're civilians.

235
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:28,252
Padua, their lives are in your hands.

236
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:30,129
[music continues]

237
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,964
I'll take care of them, sir.

238
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,467
I'll make sure they're ready.

239
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:38,137
[music swells]

240
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:44,185
[waves crashing]

241
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:50,191
[lively chatter]

242
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:53,194
[music continues]

243
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:55,279
[Emerson] I like it here.

244
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,239
[lively chatter]

245
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,617
Welcome to Velora Bay, queens!

246
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,827
Ah, correction!

247
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:05,915
- It's…
- [all] Karayom Kweens!

248
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:07,667
[giggling]

249
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,418
[pleasant music playing]

250
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:10,336
[chuckles]

251
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,962
[Atoy] Hey!

252
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:14,048
Your security here is so intense,

253
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:16,050
we feel really safe, but that's okay.

254
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,135
At least, the girls and I are safe.

255
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:20,137
Yes, correct!

256
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:21,931
[receptionist] Michael V, is that you?

257
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:23,766
Ah-- ah, well--

258
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:28,771
Joy! Just call me Joy.

259
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,022
I'm not Michael V.

260
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:32,441
There's no taping today
for <i>Bubble Gang</i> or <i>Pepito.</i>

261
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:33,734
- [Nestor] You're not sure.
- Oh, joke.

262
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:35,820
- [laughs]
- [Atoy] Thank you, mmm.

263
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:39,532
Oh, by the way… Uh, where--
where's our room, for the girls?

264
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:43,536
[receptionist] Yes. Villa number seven
has been reserved for you.

265
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:48,124
We advise you to be quiet
and no loud music, please.

266
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,793
- [others] Oh, oh.
- [receptionist] Because you are very near

267
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:55,256
the villa of Princess Putri
of the Amrati Kingdom.

268
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:56,507
- [gasps]
- [Gavin] Oh, my god.

269
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:59,802
Oh! There's a princess here!

270
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,053
- [Emerson] Really?!
- [giggles]

271
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,680
[Paldo] Can we meet her?

272
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:03,806
[giggles]

273
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:05,641
[receptionist] Unfortunately, no.

274
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:06,767
- [Paldo gasps]
- She's sick,

275
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:08,811
and she can't even make it to the party.

276
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:10,271
[others] Aww…

277
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,106
[Paldo] Sad, sad.

278
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:14,817
[receptionist] Also,
before we assist you to your villa,

279
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:18,154
we need you to sign first our NDA.

280
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:20,698
Oh! NBA! So many boys there!

281
00:12:20,781 --> 00:12:22,867
- [laughing]
- [lively chatter]

282
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,661
NDA.

283
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,830
Ahh, NDA!

284
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:29,290
[laughs]

285
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,416
What's that?

286
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:32,710
It's non-disclosure agreement, sis.

287
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,587
- Smart.
- [Kurt] Why?

288
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:36,630
What kind of party
is this going to be, ah?

289
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,466
Because I'm getting
a little excited already.

290
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,758
[laughs]

291
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:42,928
[receptionist] It's just a normal,
normal party.

292
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:45,222
But it'll be like Vegas.

293
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:46,974
Ohh!

294
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:48,309
It's like, it's like, it's like,

295
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:51,979
what happens in Velora, stays in Velora!

296
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:55,649
- [lively chatter]
- [laughing]

297
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:57,359
[receptionist]
All right, queens, are you ready?

298
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:59,487
- [others] Ready! Let's go!
- [receptionist] Let's go!

299
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,489
[lively chatter]

300
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:02,948
[Paldo] Go, girls!

301
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:05,659
[music continues]

302
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:07,036
[Emerson] Ye-hey!

303
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:11,582
[music fades]

304
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,709
The CCTV are all outside.

305
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:15,211
Inside, there's none.

306
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:17,630
Okay. Come on, hurry up.

307
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:19,590
Do your makeup and get dressed.

308
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:21,717
Remember… We are the main event;

309
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,511
we are also the main distraction.

310
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:24,762
So, we need to do our best.

311
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,013
- [Atoy] Let's go.
- Sureness, Ato--

312
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:28,307
[clears throat] I mean, uhm, exactly.

313
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:30,184
- Exactly, 'Toy.
- [Atoy] Okay.

314
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,978
After you get dressed, mingle first.

315
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:34,396
We need to keep a low profile, huh.

316
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,564
Copy?

317
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:37,775
Atoy, how can we keep a low profile?

318
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,360
Look at us.

319
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:41,111
We might end up being courted there later.

320
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,072
Oh, oh-- and the theme is Bollywood.

321
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:45,199
We'll shake it out there, joke.

322
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:49,370
Uno, you need to disable the comm system.

323
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:51,747
So the first striker team can be alerted.

324
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:54,959
Once they know,
they can penetrate the island.

325
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:56,210
They can move around,

326
00:13:56,293 --> 00:13:58,087
maybe find where the children are.

327
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,088
- -[Atoy] All right?
- Yes, sir.

328
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:00,214
Okay. Let's move, let's move!

329
00:14:00,297 --> 00:14:01,757
I'll just bring out the guns.

330
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,884
[pensive music playing]

331
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:07,555
- [clatters]
- [Karla] Ouch!

332
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:09,348
- Who's that?!
- [gasps]

333
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:11,809
- Get out!
- [rousing music playing]

334
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,311
- Karla!
- That hurt.

335
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:18,607
Son of a thread!

336
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:20,860
Karla, what are you doing here?!

337
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,653
Karla, it's dangerous here!

338
00:14:22,736 --> 00:14:24,446
Eh, why are you allowed to come?!

339
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:29,285
Sorry, Brother Atoy. I just
really want to help rescue my niece.

340
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:31,120
You, you're so stubborn, huh?

341
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:33,622
Stay here!

342
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,958
Don't leave this room, you're not coming!

343
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:37,835
Come on, come on!

344
00:14:37,918 --> 00:14:39,211
- Come on, come on, come on.
- Hurry, hurry, hurry.

345
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:42,256
Aren't you supposed to be
with the Karayom Kweens?

346
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:43,883
Why are you dressed like a bodyguard?

347
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:44,925
Who are you guarding?

348
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,012
Bodyguard?

349
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:50,890
[soft rock music playing]

350
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:55,561
You. I'll guard you.

351
00:14:55,644 --> 00:14:58,230
Me?! Eh, why me?

352
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:01,817
[music continues]

353
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:06,530
[children wailing]

354
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,411
- [goon 1] Hurry, get inside!
- [goon 2] Inside, inside!

355
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:13,621
[goon 1] Hurry!

356
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,247
[goon 1] Stay there, stay there!

357
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:16,290
You're so stubborn, huh!

358
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:18,250
- Be quiet!
- Stop it!

359
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,711
If you don't stop, I'll shoot all of you!

360
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:22,087
[children wailing]

361
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:23,672
You?! You won't stop?!

362
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,174
You're so noisy, huh!

363
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,383
[children wailing]

364
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,676
[goon 2] You, be quiet!

365
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,677
[goon 1] Stop it!

366
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,095
- Trust me…
- [goon 1] You're so irritating!

367
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,680
- …we'll escape from here.
- [goon 1] Mmph, you're stubborn, huh!

368
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,682
Huh? Escape?

369
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,809
What will you do?

370
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:37,436
Just stay quiet.

371
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:39,521
- [goon 1] Quiet!
- [goon 2] You're all so hard-headed!

372
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,231
Ibyang, what will we do?

373
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:44,568
- Just stay quiet.
- [goon 2] You're crying again.

374
00:15:45,569 --> 00:15:46,403
Uh…

375
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:50,032
Brother, brother,
can I go to the bathroom?

376
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:52,326
I really need to pee.

377
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:53,619
Go pee in the corner.

378
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:55,788
Ah--

379
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:57,706
Uhm…

380
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,249
Eh, it's not pee,

381
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:00,876
It's number two, actually!

382
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,670
You're just fooling us.

383
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,047
Oh. No, promise, ah-

384
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:07,716
Gosh! It's coming out, it's coming out!

385
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,843
- [goon 2] She might make a mess here.
- Come on, come on, come on!

386
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:10,803
I'll go with you!

387
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:11,720
[suspicious music playing]

388
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:12,680
Hurry!

389
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:13,889
[music continues]

390
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:16,225
[goon 1] Stop it already! You're so noisy!

391
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:18,310
[music fades]

392
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:26,276
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

393
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:50,300
Hmm, look at these people.

394
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:51,635
Wait, wait, wait.

395
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:53,762
[music fades]

396
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,097
Look at that.

397
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,265
[mysterious music playing]

398
00:16:56,348 --> 00:17:01,437
<i>The court has released a warrant of arrest</i>
<i>for Former Mayor Rizaldo Coloma,</i>

399
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,772
<i>the alleged bagman of corrupt senators.</i>

400
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,650
That's Rizaldo Coloma, right?

401
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:10,237
He's the corrupt mayor
and the… the bagman!

402
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,448
[music continues]

403
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,658
That's why we have an NDA.

404
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:17,327
- [gasps]
- So we won't say who's here.

405
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:20,539
[music continues]

406
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:22,082
Can you believe that?

407
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,084
[Emerson chuckles]

408
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:28,130
So that's why.
That bastard is hiding here.

409
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:29,631
- Hey.
- Would be nice to smash--

410
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,633
- [sneaky music playing]
- You're even eating here.

411
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,802
[mumbles] I'm hiding it already, eh.

412
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,095
Stop that.

413
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:37,723
[somber music playing]

414
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:49,359
[tense music playing]

415
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:54,907
Atoy, my dear…

416
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,159
where's Uno?

417
00:17:58,285 --> 00:17:59,536
He split from us earlier.

418
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,081
We talked through the earpiece.

419
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,668
[music swells]

420
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,909
Eh, where's Karla?

421
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:46,959
[sneaky music playing]

422
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:05,477
Raise it a little higher,
raise it a little higher.

423
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:06,728
[Atoy clears throat]

424
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:08,772
Hello, Ma'am.

425
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:12,234
[music continues]

426
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:15,112
My dear, you look so interesting.

427
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,488
I'm Mrs. Villaforte.

428
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:17,656
And you are?

429
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:22,494
Uh, um… apologies for not introducing her.

430
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:26,248
She is Princess Putri of Amrati.

431
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,500
She is a princess?

432
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,878
No wonder she looks magnificent.

433
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:32,421
Thank you.

434
00:19:32,504 --> 00:19:34,173
[tense music playing]

435
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,019
[Atoy clears throat]

436
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:49,146
Did I hear princess?

437
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:51,857
Yes. Meet the princess of Amrati.

438
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,275
- Oh.
- Excuse me.

439
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,235
It's very nice to meet you.

440
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:58,071
You know, my husband
would've loved to meet you too.

441
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,616
[heavy music playing]

442
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:03,702
Too bad, we're here on business.

443
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:06,747
Ah, what kind of business?

444
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:09,124
You do monkey business?

445
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:12,961
[music intensifies]

446
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:17,257
Excuse me.

447
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:19,801
[music swells]

448
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,061
[music fades]

449
00:20:33,148 --> 00:20:37,986
[tense music playing]

450
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,659
My necklace?

451
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:48,288
[music continues]

452
00:20:51,667 --> 00:20:53,418
[music fades]

453
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:59,258
[soft rock music playing]

454
00:21:13,188 --> 00:21:15,732
Rizaldo Coloma, the mayor in hiding?

455
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:16,858
[Mercado] Yes.

456
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:19,736
The corrupt mayor, bagman of the senators.

457
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:22,364
So, you're here too, you animal?

458
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:23,949
[music continues]

459
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:26,243
You even joined forces, you two demons.

460
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:28,954
[music continues]

461
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,500
Mr. Ambassador.

462
00:21:33,583 --> 00:21:35,419
Oh, Senator.

463
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,421
- How--
- Do you remember my wife?

464
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:38,672
Yes, ah--

465
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:43,719
[suspicious music playing]

466
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:45,345
- Hey!
- [thuds]

467
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,930
Aren't you done yet?!

468
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:48,932
Eh, I'll take even longer.

469
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,768
You're disturbing me, eh.

470
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:53,979
I can't concentrate.

471
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:58,400
[music continues]

472
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:02,487
[goon 1] Let's finish this.

473
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,031
Put medicine in that batch.

474
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:06,491
[goon 2] What's this for? Vitamins?

475
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:08,410
[goon 1] Sleeping pills.

476
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:10,078
So the children will sleep.

477
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,496
So they'll be easier
to load onto the ship.

478
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,998
They won't wake up until tomorrow.

479
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:15,500
[music fades]

480
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:18,962
[device blips]

481
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:22,382
[ominous music playing]

482
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:32,517
- [swishes]
- [groans]

483
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:37,272
Ouch.

484
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,150
- [groans]
- [music continues]

485
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,902
[goon 2] Oh, your food!

486
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:44,696
At least the children
have something to eat!

487
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,781
[goon 2] Do you want some?

488
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:46,948
Take some.

489
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:48,742
[goon 1] No.

490
00:22:48,825 --> 00:22:50,494
[goon 2] Hey, eat up!

491
00:22:50,577 --> 00:22:51,745
[goon 1] Be quiet!

492
00:22:51,828 --> 00:22:53,705
Here's your food!
You don't even want to eat!

493
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:54,831
[heavy music playing]

494
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:56,083
Eat now!

495
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:58,210
- [music continues]
- [children sobbing]

496
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:15,393
[tense music playing]

497
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:29,616
Surprised to see me?

498
00:23:29,699 --> 00:23:32,035
[ominous music playing]

499
00:23:32,869 --> 00:23:34,037
[Red] It's a small world.

500
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,124
Turns out you wronged both me and Samir.

501
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:39,251
Where are the children?

502
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:43,713
[tense music playing]

503
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:52,180
- [electronic blipping]
- [intense music playing]

504
00:23:57,727 --> 00:24:00,105
You want to get back at me, don't you?
Revenge!

505
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:01,773
[thumping]

506
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:06,653
[grunting & groaning]

507
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:11,241
[grunting & groaning]

508
00:24:11,324 --> 00:24:12,701
[theme music playing]

509
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:14,828
This is Tonet and her brother.

510
00:24:14,911 --> 00:24:16,204
How did they end up here?

511
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,789
Madame, maybe you're being haunted.

512
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:20,167
That's the one
you killed at the mall, right?

513
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,710
- [music continues]
- [groans]

514
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:23,920
UP NEXT

515
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:25,589
- Tatoy!
- [Atoy] My child?

516
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:28,884
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

517
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:32,012
<i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪</i>

518
00:24:32,095 --> 00:24:33,555
<i>♪ Holding the scissors ♪</i>

519
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:34,848
Ibyang!

520
00:24:34,931 --> 00:24:37,559
